            <div xml:id="d771">

                <pb facs="0987" n="873" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg873"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860m.01/132: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Herrick</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-06-30T18:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 30, 1922—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 30—4:35
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>271. My 234, January 23, 1920.<anchor n="86" xml:id="d771-f1"/> Conference of
                    Ambassadors at 183rd meeting held this morning decided that Principal Allied
                    Powers would recognize Lithuania <hi rendition="#italic">de jure</hi>. This is
                    independent of determination of status of Memel to study which question a
                    committee of Conference secretaries is to be appointed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herrick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
